<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Milas</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mylasa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Milas is a town in Muğla province, south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, on the site of ancient Mylasa, the capital of Caria under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hecatomnid-dynasty">Hecatomnid dynasty</a>. In the late thirteenth century it was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> raiders and became a chief town of the Menteshe <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a>, whose rulers built mosques there. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-battuta">Ibn Battuta</a> visited it in the 1330s and praised its ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orhan">Orhan</a> Bey.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/milas.jpg" alt="Milas" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Emirr · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mu%C4%9Fla_location_Milas.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
